magpiesettlertip=Lives in the Spire Village around the Old Warden Spire. Recruit price: coins and the Bonded Lockbox from the Skyway Toll-House. Works Trading missions and runs sky voyages.
haldasettlertip=Lives in the Spire Village around the Old Warden Spire. Recruit price: coins and the Mother from the Grange Cellar. Works Fishing.
ossiansettlertip=Lives in the Spire Village around the Old Warden Spire. Recruit price: coins and the Storm Lens Core from the Stormveil Test Range. Works Crafting and Hauling.
eveleensettlertip=Lives in the Spire Village around the Old Warden Spire, beside her Eden bed. Her fee is waived once she has her three Eden fruit. Works Farming, Forestry and Fertilising.
mortimersettlertip=Lives in the Spire Village around the Old Warden Spire. His fee is waived once his rites are done. Works Hauling, Crafting and Hunting.
caspernsettlertip=Lives in the Spire Village around the Old Warden Spire. His fee is waived once his forge burns again. Works Crafting and Hauling, and nothing outdoors.
eleanorsettlertip=Lives in the Spire Village around the Old Warden Spire. She never comes to you - you decide whether she stays. Works Husbandry.
knottsettlertip=Lives in the Spire Village around the Old Warden Spire, in the house with the red door. Works Trading, and nothing outdoors.
ivessettlertip=Lives in the Spire Village around the Old Warden Spire. His fee is waived once the vigil is kept. Works Crafting and Hauling, and buys everything the Quiet Reach gives up.

// --- Ives, the Verger ---
ivestalkpitch=Things end up out here. People too, in the end. Somebody has to write down what they were, and I appear to be somebody.
ivestalk1=Nothing is buried here. It is only put down. There is a difference, and I mind it.
ivestalk2=One of them walks the same eleven steps every evening. I have counted. I have not interrupted.
ivestalk3=The gold goes dark out here. Everything the sky was proud of goes dark out here.
ivestalk4=I keep a list. I have never finished a page of it.
ivesasksvigil=Bring me grave salt and spirit moss and I will lay them properly. Fourteen and ten. They have waited long enough.
ivesvigildone=There. They can stop walking now. Take the bars - the Warden owed me and I never wanted them.

// --- Mortimer's rites ---
mortimerasksrites=There are twelve out there I have not been able to reach. Bring me soul thread for the shrouds and bonewood for the boxes, and I will go get them.
mortimerritesdone=Done, and done properly. Keep your money. Keep the bars instead, and keep me.

// --- Caspern's forge ---
caspernasksforge=My fire went out and I have not been able to relight it. Spectral ore to feed it, veil essence to quench it. Then we can talk about what you want made.
caspernforgedone=Listen to that. That is the sound I told you about. Take these, and do not pay me anything again.

// --- Eveleen ---
eveleentalkpitch=I came up the long way, looking for a garden somebody told me was still growing. I have not found it. But you have soil, and I have seeds nobody else up here will sell you.
eveleentalk1=Everything grows if you are patient and ruthless in the right order.
eveleentalk2=That patch is thirsty. No, do not water it. It is thirsty for something else.
eveleentalk3=I keep three seeds I have never planted. I would like to know what they are before I find out.
eveleentalk4=A garden is not decoration. A garden is an argument you are having with the ground.
eveleenasksplants=Bring me one of each: an Eden Berry, a Moon Melon, a Sun Grape. Prove to me it still grows.
eveleenplantsdone=So. It still grows out there. Good.

// --- Mortimer ---
mortimertalkpitch=You have dead to keep and nowhere to keep them. I have a spade, a hat, and no particular hurry. We can help each other.
mortimertalk1=A settlement without a graveyard is a settlement that has not been honest yet.
mortimertalk2=I hunt as well. Somebody has to bring things in, and I am already dressed for it.
mortimertalk3=Do not thank me. Thank me later. Much later, ideally.
mortimertalk4=Every stone I sell is blank. What you write on it is your business.

// --- Caspern ---
casperntalkpitch=I work metal that remembers. It is not a trick and it is not cheap. Build me a forge and I will show you what a bar is supposed to sound like.
casperntalk1=Cold iron forgets. This does not.
casperntalk2=No, I will not go outside. The fire is in here.
casperntalk3=Every bar I draw has somebody's patience in it. Usually mine.
casperntalk4=Bring me ore. Bring me dust. Do not bring me questions about where the dust came from.

// --- Eleanor ---
eleanortalkpitch=I do not know why I am still here. I thought I did. If you would rather I stayed, I will stay - I am good with animals, and they do not mind what I am.
eleanortalk1=I remember a kitchen. I do not remember whose.
eleanortalk2=The goats are not frightened of me. That is worth a great deal.
eleanortalk3=Do not be sad on my account. I am not sure I can be.
eleanortalk4=Sometimes I catch myself waiting. I have stopped asking for what.
eleanorneedessence=Not enough of me yet. <have> of <need>.
eleanorfarewell=Oh. Oh, so that was all it was.
eleanorpassedon=Eleanor thins out like breath on cold glass.\nWhere she stood there is a small lantern, still warm.

// --- Knott ---
knotttalkpitch=Every door in this yard is convinced it leads somewhere. I have believed them for longer than is reasonable. You look like someone who might prove one of us right.
knotttalk1=Going somewhere?
knotttalk2=A door that opens onto nothing is still a door. It just has manners.
knotttalk3=I do not sell keys to doors I have not tested. Test enough of them and you stop needing keys.
knotttalk4=Somebody has to keep asking where they lead. Might as well be me.
knottasksdoor=If you truly think one of these leads somewhere, prove it. Bring me what a door like that would need.
knottdoordone=Ha! So it does lead somewhere. Take this - you argued it out of me.

[quests]
// --- Eveleen, the Eden chain ---
swhedenreachtitle=Into the Garden
swhedenreachdesc=Eveleen talks about a garden further out, greener than anything in the Skyreach. She wants to know whether it still grows.
swhedenreachobj=Set foot in the Garden of Eden (600-2,880 tiles from the spire), then tell Eveleen in the Spire Village.
swhspeaktoeveleen=Speak with Eveleen.
swhedenplantstitle=A Taste of Eden
swhedenplantsdesc=Eveleen wants proof the garden is real: an Eden Berry, a Moon Melon, and a Sun Grape.
swhedenplantsreward=3x Knowledge Cutting + 10x Stormsteel Bar

// --- Eleanor ---
swheleanortitle=Why She Stayed
swheleanordesc=Something keeps Eleanor here after everyone else has gone on. She does not know why. Maybe you can help her decide what to do about it.
swheleanorobj=Speak with Eleanor. Hold Veil Essence to help her pass on, or come empty-handed to ask her to stay.
swheleanorreward=Pass on: Will-o'-Wisp Lantern + 10x Spiritsteel Bar. Stay: she joins your settlement + 10x Spiritsteel Bar.
swhspeaktoeleanor=Speak with Eleanor.

// --- Mr. Knott, the Crooked chain ---
swhcrookedarrivaltitle=A Door That Goes Somewhere
swhcrookedarrivaldesc=Mr. Knott swears that past the bend there is a yard full of doors, and that one of them leads somewhere. He wants you to see it.
swhcrookedarrivalobj=Set foot in the Crooked Beyond (from about 4,200 tiles out), then tell Mr. Knott in the Spire Village.
swhspeaktoknott=Speak with Mr. Knott.
swhsteinfeldvigiltitle=The Vigil
swhsteinfeldvigildesc=Ives keeps the Quiet Reach, and the Quiet Reach does not stay kept. The ones who walk out here are not haunting anybody - they were simply never laid down. He knows what it takes and has run out of both.
swhsteinfeldvigilreward=Ives joins your settlement for free + 12x Stormsteel Bar
swhspeaktoives=Speak with Ives.

// --- Mortimer, the Aftergarden ---
swhmortimerritestitle=The Last Rites
swhmortimerritesdesc=Mortimer can name every grave in the Aftergarden and reach almost none of them. A shroud is thread and a coffin is wood, and he is short of both.
swhmortimerritesreward=Mortimer joins your settlement for free + 6x Spiritsteel Bar
swhspeaktomortimer=Speak with Mortimer.

// --- Caspern, the Aftergarden ---
swhcaspernforgetitle=The Cold Forge
swhcaspernforgedesc=The Spirit Smith's fire has gone out. Spectral ore feeds it and veil essence quenches it, and the second only drops where the fog is thickest.
swhcaspernforgereward=Caspern joins your settlement for free + 6x Spiritsteel Bar
swhspeaktocaspern=Speak with Caspern.

// --- Mr. Knott, the Crooked chain (continued) ---
swhcrookeddoortitle=Convince the Door
swhcrookeddoordesc=Mr. Knott has spent longer than anyone believing one of these doors can be convinced to lead somewhere. Bring him what a door like that would need.
swhcrookeddoorreward=Zephyr Harness + 12x Spiritsteel Bar + 6x Reality Shard

