[quests]
swhkeyskyreachtitle=The Watchfire
swhkeyskyreachdesc=The Warden can build a watchfire that the Skyreach's own summoning stones will answer to - if you bring him the storm to light it with.
swhkeyskyreachreward=Skyreach Watchfire + 4x Stormdisc + Skywatch Hood + 4x Stormsteel Bar
swhkeyedentitle=The Moon Arch
swhkeyedendesc=Eden guards its sap and its pollen with teeth and stings. Take both from the garden, and two fangs off the Bloom Maws that bite, and the Sky Warden will raise you an arch that its stones recognise.
swhkeyedenreward=Eden Moon Arch + Galehowl + Warden's Mantle + 5x Stormsteel Bar
swhkeysteinfeldtitle=The Mourning Angel
swhkeysteinfelddesc=Steinfeld is nothing but pale stone and the echoes trapped in it. Bring back enough of each and the Warden will raise one of its angels in your own settlement.
swhkeysteinfeldreward=Steinfeld Mourning Angel + Tempest Edge + Warden's Boots + 6x Stormsteel Bar
swhkeyghostrealmtitle=The Raven Perch
swhkeyghostrealmdesc=Nothing comes out of the Aftergarden that the fog has not already touched. Carry back its bonewood and its spectral ore, and the Warden will set a raven over your gate.
swhkeyghostrealmreward=Aftergarden Raven Perch + Spiritsteel Reaver + Stormsteel Vambrace + 6x Spiritsteel Bar
swhkeycrookedbeyondtitle=A Door of Your Own
swhkeycrookedbeyonddesc=Every door in the Crooked Beyond leads somewhere it should not. Bring the Warden its wood and its shards and he will hang you one that does it on purpose.
swhkeycrookedbeyondreward=Knott's Crooked Door + Gravewind Bow + Aurora Locket + 8x Spiritsteel Bar
swhkeyhelltitle=Everything Appears to Be in Order
swhkeyhelldesc=Hell does not open for anybody without the paperwork. The Warden cannot get you a form, so he will settle for proof you have been out that far: the Crooked Beyond, twice over.
swhkeyhellreward=Infernal Seal + 16x Spiritsteel Bar
[misc]
regionkeyneedsettlement=A key piece only holds where people live. Stand it up inside your settlement.
regionkeyunlocked=The key piece settles into the ground: <key>.\nSomewhere far out, a cold stone warms.
wardenkeyaskskyreach=There is a way to call the things that sleep out there - but they only answer their own kind. Bring me the storm, and two more golem hearts, and I will build you a watchfire.
wardenkeydoneskyreach=That will burn. Set it down at home, where the walls are yours.
wardenkeyaskeden=Eden next, then. Sap and pollen, and two fangs off the flowers that bite - none of it will be handed to you.
wardenkeydoneeden=Green things, and still warm. Take the arch - it knows the way its own stones are cut.
wardenkeyasksteinfeld=Steinfeld keeps its dead standing. Bring me pale stone and the echoes in it, and two mourning bands off the statues that weep, and I will raise you one of its angels.
wardenkeydonesteinfeld=She is heavier than she looks. Give her ground she will be left alone on.
wardenkeyaskghostrealm=The Aftergarden, now, and you will want your chalk before you go. Bonewood and spectral ore - and two collars off the brides who wander there.
wardenkeydoneghostrealm=A bird for the dead, and it will sit anywhere you put it. That is more than most of them will do.
wardenkeyaskcrookedbeyond=Last one, and the worst. The Crooked Beyond has a door for everything. Bring me the wood and the shards, and two horns out of the doors that bite, and I will hang you one that behaves.
wardenkeydonecrookedbeyond=There. A door of your own, and it opens on purpose. That is the whole set.
wardenkeyaskhell=One more. There is one further out than the doors, and it keeps records. Bring me twice what the Crooked cost you and I will stamp you something it recognises.
wardenkeydonehell=Alive, dead and unreasonable. Everything appears to be in order. Do not lose it.

