lore0atitle=The Skywatch
lore0a=Once an order kept watch over the clouds from the spire and its beacon. The order stopped answering, its freight stopped landing, and one keeper stayed on to keep the light burning, because somebody had to.
lore0ahint=Unlocked by: meeting the Warden.
lore0btitle=Siggi and Peanut
lore0b=The spire's cats always sat on the warm vat in Halda's cellar. When the tower emptied they went wild in the storm and on the shoals - but a cat never quite forgets where the basket stood.
lore0bhint=Unlocked by: bringing a spire cat home.
lore0ctitle=An island at anchor
lore0c=The spire island drifted for as long as anyone remembers. Anchored with your metal and stone, it is the one fixed point in the sky - and from here the Warden can start making keys.
lore0chint=Unlocked by: anchoring the island.
lore1atitle=Uncomfortably perfect
lore1a=Everything in Eden grows too well. The fruit is too large, the water too blue, the grass too tall to see what moves in it. Beauty here is not a promise; it is bait.
lore1ahint=Unlocked by: setting foot in Eden.
lore1btitle=The Tree of Knowledge
lore1b=Eveleen came looking for a garden that was said to still grow, and found only the tree. Its cuttings take root anywhere - which, she says, is exactly the problem.
lore1bhint=Unlocked by: bringing Eveleen her proof.
lore2atitle=Where the sky stops working
lore2a=Things end up in Steinfeld that no longer quite belong to the sky. The clouds go grey, the statues crack, and the gold the Skywatch was proud of darkens out here like everything else.
lore2ahint=Unlocked by: walking into Steinfeld.
lore2btitle=Eleven steps
lore2b=The ones who walk the Quiet Reach are not haunting anybody. They were simply never laid down. One of them walks the same eleven steps every evening; Ives counts along and has never interrupted him.
lore2bhint=Unlocked by: keeping the vigil with Ives.
lore3atitle=The fog
lore3a=The fog is not weather. It is the border of the afterlife, and it strips anyone still alive down to the soul, one breath at a time.
lore3ahint=Unlocked by: touching the fog wall.
lore3btitle=Marked for passage
lore3b=The Ghost Guide was a surveyor once and still counts things. When he breathes on you, the fog counts you among its own - and lets you through.
lore3bhint=Unlocked by: receiving the Veil Mark.
lore3ctitle=The dead have problems too
lore3c=A shroud short of thread, a forge gone cold, a woman who cannot remember whose kitchen she misses. The Aftergarden is not peaceful; it is simply busy with things nobody alive thinks about.
lore3chint=Unlocked by: helping one of the Aftergarden's dead.
lore4atitle=The rules decay
lore4a=Out here the paths run visibly wrong, stairs lead nowhere and windows lie on the floor. After death it is not only the landscape that falls apart.
lore4ahint=Unlocked by: walking into the Crooked Beyond.
lore4btitle=A door that means it
lore4b=Every door in the Yard leads somewhere it should not. Mr. Knott only ever wanted one that did it on purpose. Now there is one - and he would like it noted that he was right.
lore4bhint=Unlocked by: convincing the door with Mr. Knott.
lore5atitle=Everything appears to be in order
lore5a=Hell is not a fire landscape. It is a functioning society with counters, forms and a waiting room - and beside one counter a skeleton that has evidently been waiting four hundred years.
lore5ahint=Unlocked by: reaching Hell.
lore5btitle=The Infernal Seal
lore5b=No form could be found, so the Warden took proof instead: the Crooked Beyond, twice over. Heaven, death and hell keep their books in the same ledger - the seal is only the stamp that says so.
lore5bhint=Unlocked by: earning the Infernal Seal.
// ---- Spire Village and quest ladder (chapter-03-spire-village.md) ----
[quests]
swhladderposttitle=Undelivered Post
swhladderpostdesc=Magpie flew freight for the Skywatch until the road went quiet. Her Ledger of Undelivered Post is still in the office of the Skyway Toll-House - behind the Tollwright who guards the till.
swhladderpostreward=Magpie's Satchel (accessory: wider pickup range, more stamina)
swhladderroundtitle=The Cellar Yeast
swhladderrounddesc=Halda wants to start her cellar again. The Mother still lives in the Grange Cellar, but without feed she is nothing: cloudberries and wind wheat from the Driftlands, aurora petals from the Aurora Shoals.
swhladderroundreward=3x Storm Brew, then on sale in her shop
swhladderprototypetitle=What Prototype Nine Was Built From
swhladderprototypedesc=Ossian wants to understand what is still running on the Stormveil Test Range. For that he needs what it was built from: storm glass, storm shards and fulgurite from the Stormveil.
swhladderprototypereward=Reader's Lens (accessory: shows ore, faster mining)
swhladdercidertitle=Paradise Cider
swhladderciderdesc=Halda has heard about the Garden and wants to start a cider nobody up here knows: paradise apples, paradise coconuts and Eden sap - the Hedge Labyrinth keeps the apples, the Bloom Maws the sap.
swhladderciderreward=3x Paradise Cider, then on sale in her shop
swhladdercontrabandtitle=Contraband from the Garden
swhladdercontrabanddesc=Magpie has buyers for serpent scales and venom fangs - and needs the Skyway Writ from the Toll-House so the cargo gets through on every road.
swhladdercontrabandreward=Magpie's sky voyages: every open route +15% success
swhladderechotitle=The Echo in the Archive
swhladderechodesc=In Steinfeld voices have turned to stone. Ossian wants to archive them: ten echo shards, and a mourning band from a Stone Mourner.
swhladderechoreward=Echo Conch (accessory: +25% crit damage, +3% crit)
swhladderstepstitle=The Eleven Steps
swhladderstepsdesc=One of the dead in Steinfeld walks the same eleven steps every evening. Ives wants to lay the path for him: eleven each of grave salt, spirit moss and pale stone.
swhladderstepsreward=Verger's Lantern (accessory: shows enemies, +30 health)
swhladdermemorytitle=Metal That Remembers
swhladdermemorydesc=Caspern wants to forge a blade that remembers something. He needs a soul collar from a Mourning Bride, and bonewood and ectoplasm from the Aftergarden.
swhladdermemoryreward=The Remembering Blade (greatsword, 186 damage)
swhladdershroudstitle=Shrouds for the Feast
swhladdershroudsdesc=The Wedding Feast in the Ghost Realm never ended. Mortimer wants to cover the guests at last: ten soul thread and six veil essence.
swhladdershroudsreward=Mourning Brooch (accessory: +8 armour, +25 health)
swhladderseedstitle=Seeds I Never Planted
swhladderseedsdesc=Eveleen has three seeds she never planted. In the Crooked Beyond eye seeds grow that can see what a seed wants to become. She wants six - and three knowledge cuttings.
swhladderseedsreward=Root Crown (accessory: +60 health, +1 combat regeneration)
swhladdershellstitle=A Door with Manners
swhladdershellsdesc=Mr. Knott is building a door that behaves. For it he needs eight striped shells and the horn of a Door Mimic.
swhladdershellsreward=Knott's Key Ring (accessory: faster dash, +10% speed)
swhladderformtitle=Form 666-B
swhladderformdesc=Hell keeps books, and Ossian wants to know what is in them. The form for that asks for proof in Hell-sized amounts: sixteen reality shards, twenty-four oddwood, thirty charwood.
swhladderformreward=The Auditor's Seal (accessory: +10% damage, +5% crit)
