// ---- Dorian made legible (concept-nightbound-dorian.md 3.1-3.5, E1-E5) ----
[mobmsg]
doctortalk6=Your night guest... I always keep something against blood fever. Come to me, or buy a tincture and do it yourself.
doctortalk7=Two marks on the neck and pale as milk? That is not a cold. That is Dorian, and it is curable.

[misc]
swhdoctorbittenoption=Treat the bitten (<count>, <price> coins)
swhdoctorbitten=<count> of your people have bite marks on the neck. I have something for that - it is not a cold.
swhdorianoption=About your thirst
swhdorianfeed=Give him a Blood Vial
swhdorianfed=Thank you. That buys your people a night.
swhdorianthirst0=I am sated. Nobody needs to worry tonight.
swhdorianthirst1=I am thirsty. Not yet dangerous.
swhdorianthirst2=I am very thirsty. Fill the bowl, or I go hunting further out.
swhdorianthirst3=I will have to bite someone tonight. I would rather not.
swhdorianreportquiet=Last night was quiet.
swhdorianreport=Last night I drained <drained> animals. <thralls> got up again.
swhdorianreportbit=<report> And I bit: <names>.
swhdorianquest1=Teach me to walk by day (<vials> Blood Vials, <essence> Veil Essence)
swhdorianquest2=Teach me to need no night (<vials> Blood Vials)
swhdorianquestdone1=The sun no longer slows me. I am as fast by day as I am by night.
swhdorianquestdone2=I no longer need the night. From now on I sleep only when I am tired, and never for long.
swhdorianstage1=I walk by day now. The sun no longer slows me.
swhdorianstage2=I walk by day and by night. I sleep only when I am tired.
swhdorianturn=Turn <name> into a night settler (<vials> Blood Vials)
swhdorianunturn=Give <name> the daylight back
swhdorianturned=It is done. <name> will sleep by day and work by night from now on.
swhdorianunturned=<name> belongs to the day again. The night lets go.
vampirebowl=From the bowl. Better so.
bloodbowlstock=The bowl holds <count> of <max> Blood Vials.\nDorian drinks from it at night before he would bite anyone.

[ui]
swhnotificationbloodfever=Dorian has bitten someone: blood fever
swhnotificationbloodfeverhelp=Slower and weaker for a day. The Doctor cures it, or a Blood-Fever Tincture; a filled Blood Bowl stops the next bite.

[object]
bloodbowl=Blood Bowl

[itemtooltip]
bloodbowltip=Put Blood Vials in. Dorian drinks from it at night instead of biting a settler.

[journal]
whylabel=Why:
wherelabel=Where:
openslabel=Opens:
whyfindspire=The Warden is the one who knows this sky. Every later quest up here - the cats, the anchor, the keys to the bosses - comes from him.
opensfindspire=The Last Sky Warden: recruiting him
whyrecruitwarden=Only a Warden who lives in your settlement keeps handing you quests wherever you meet him, and his hire lights the spire's beacon again.
opensrecruitwarden=The Spire Cats, with both cat lairs marked on your map
whycats=The cats belong to the tower. Once both sleep in the basket, the Warden trusts you with the island itself - and the Cat Basket exists nowhere else.
openscats=Anchor the Island; the Warden sells the Cat Basket and garlands from then on
whyanchor=The spire island drifts. Anchored, it stays where you left it, and the Warden's own chain is finished - only then does he start on the keys to the realms' bosses.
opensanchor=The first region key (The Watchfire); the Warden sells the Cloud Glaive and banner from then on
whyghostchalk=The fog past Steinfeld kills the living (Soul Exposure). The chalk draws the séance circle whose Ghost Guide makes the fog let you through.
opensghostchalk=The Veil Mark
whykeyskyreach=A key piece stood up in your settlement wakes that realm's Summoning Stones. Without it they stay inert and the realm's boss cannot be called.
openskeyskyreach=The Skyreach's Summoning Stones (its boss), and the next key: The Moon Arch
whykeyeden=Eden's Summoning Stones only answer an arch grown from Eden's own sap and pollen. Stand it up at home to wake them.
openskeyeden=Eden's Summoning Stones (its boss), and the next key: The Mourning Angel
whykeysteinfeld=Steinfeld's Summoning Stones sleep until one of its angels stands in your settlement.
openskeysteinfeld=Steinfeld's Summoning Stones (its boss), and the next key: The Raven Perch
whykeyghostrealm=The Aftergarden's Summoning Stones only wake for a raven perch made from its bonewood and spectral ore.
openskeyghostrealm=The Aftergarden's Summoning Stones (its boss), and the next key: A Door of Your Own
whykeycrookedbeyond=The Crooked Beyond's Summoning Stones answer to a door - one of its own, standing in your settlement.
openskeycrookedbeyond=The Crooked Beyond's Summoning Stones (its boss), and the last key: Everything Appears to Be in Order
whykeyhell=Hell's Infernal Summoning Forge wants the paperwork: the Infernal Seal, stood up in your settlement.
openskeyhell=The Infernal Summoning Forge and Hell's boss - the last rung of the ladder
whyswhedenreach=Eveleen will not believe the Garden still grows until someone has stood in it. Her Eden Grass Seed is the first piece of Eden you can grow at home.
opensswhedenreach=Her next task: A Taste of Eden. It is also one of the steps Chapter III - Steinfeld waits for.
whyswhedenplants=Three fruits only the Garden grows are the proof Eveleen wants. Once she has them, she no longer asks a price to join you.
opensswhedenplants=Eveleen joins your settlement for free; her last task, Seeds I Never Planted, once Chapter V is open. Also one of the steps Chapter III waits for.
whyswhladderseeds=Eye seeds from the Crooked Beyond can see what a seed wants to become - and Eveleen still does not know what her three are. The Knowledge Cuttings from A Taste of Eden go into it too.
opensswhladderseeds=Eveleen's last task. It is one of the steps Chapter VI - Hell waits for.
whyswhsteinfeldvigil=The dead in Steinfeld walk because nobody ever laid them down. Ives knows how, but has run out of what it takes - bring it, and he no longer asks a price to join you.
opensswhsteinfeldvigil=Ives joins your settlement for free; his next task: The Eleven Steps. Also one of the steps Chapter IV - the Ghost Realm waits for.
whyswhladdersteps=One of Steinfeld's dead walks the same eleven steps every evening. Laying the path lets him stand still at last.
opensswhladdersteps=Ives's last task. It is one of the steps Chapter IV - the Ghost Realm waits for.
whyswhmortimerrites=Mortimer knows every grave in the Aftergarden but lacks the thread and wood for shrouds and coffins. Bring them, and he no longer asks a price to join you.
opensswhmortimerrites=Mortimer joins your settlement for free; his next task: Shrouds for the Feast. Also one of the steps Chapter V - the Crooked Beyond waits for.
whyswhladdershrouds=The Wedding Feast in the Ghost Realm never ended. Mortimer wants to cover its guests at last.
opensswhladdershrouds=Mortimer's last task. It is one of the steps Chapter V - the Crooked Beyond waits for.
whyswhcaspernforge=The Spirit Smith's fire has gone out. Relit, it burns for you: Caspern no longer asks a price to join you.
opensswhcaspernforge=Caspern joins your settlement for free; his next task: Metal That Remembers. Also one of the steps Chapter V - the Crooked Beyond waits for.
whyswhladdermemory=Caspern wants to forge a blade that remembers something, and the Mourning Brides still wear what it needs.
opensswhladdermemory=Caspern's last task. It is one of the steps Chapter V - the Crooked Beyond waits for.
whyswheleanor=Eleanor stayed behind when everyone else went on, and does not know why. What happens to her is your choice.
opensswheleanor=Either she passes on and leaves you her lantern, or she moves into your settlement. The next chapter does not wait for this - it may stay open.
whyswhcrookedarrival=Mr. Knott swears a yard full of doors lies past the bend and wants a witness. The Reality Shards come from there.
opensswhcrookedarrival=His next task: Convince the Door. Also one of the steps Chapter VI - Hell waits for.
whyswhcrookeddoor=Mr. Knott believes one of the Door Yard's doors can be convinced to lead somewhere. Bring what such a door would need.
opensswhcrookeddoor=His next task: A Door with Manners, and the Chronicle entry A door that means it. Also one of the steps Chapter VI - Hell waits for.
whyswhladdershells=Mr. Knott is teaching a door manners - striped shells for the frame, and a horn from a door that tried to eat you.
opensswhladdershells=Mr. Knott's last task. It is one of the steps Chapter VI - Hell waits for.

[misc]
wardendialogtask=Your task: <title>
wardendialogjournal=Details are in your Sky Chronicle.
wardendialogcats=Two cats came with this tower, and two cats are out in the weather. They will not come for me any more. They might come for you, with something to eat.
wardendialoganchor=The cats are home; the island is not. It drifts. Bring me metal and stone and I will set it where it belongs.

